WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.858 --> 00:00:03.869
- [Tim] I've flown past mach one

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:06.377
several times off a carrier.

00:00:06.377 --> 00:00:08.101
The most exciting portion of it

00:00:08.101 --> 00:00:10.309
is getting shot off the front end.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:12.477
The body is experiencing this different

00:00:12.477 --> 00:00:14.650
feel to it completely.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.610
From zero to 150 miles an hour in about

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.034
two and a half seconds.

00:00:19.034 --> 00:00:21.274
I'm Tim Hibbits, I am a pilot,

00:00:21.274 --> 00:00:25.274
and I have flown faster
than the speed of sound.

00:00:27.205 --> 00:00:29.727
When you're sitting on
the carrier at night,

00:00:29.727 --> 00:00:31.986
you're right across from
the island which has

00:00:31.986 --> 00:00:35.069
all these big, orange, sodium lights.

00:00:37.165 --> 00:00:39.855
It's this orange glow
that's palling everything

00:00:39.855 --> 00:00:42.055
and everybody's almost monochromatic

00:00:42.055 --> 00:00:45.638
and outside of that,
it's just pitch black.

00:00:47.183 --> 00:00:50.194
As soon as they punch the button,

00:00:50.194 --> 00:00:52.472
and you start off on the catapult,

00:00:52.472 --> 00:00:54.514
you've got these lights
now that were around you

00:00:54.514 --> 00:00:56.866
and now they're streaking past you.

00:00:56.866 --> 00:00:58.980
You body is pulled back into the seat.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.151
Your hearing is now assaulted.

00:01:01.151 --> 00:01:03.213
You're under these extreme forces.

00:01:03.213 --> 00:01:06.060
Anything that could go wrong now

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.227
could be really disastrous
in the next few seconds.

00:01:11.082 --> 00:01:15.471
Suddenly you reach the
end of the catapult.

00:01:15.471 --> 00:01:18.773
And all you're left with is hanging out,

00:01:18.773 --> 00:01:22.940
for an instant you can
feel, hear, and see nothing.

00:01:24.813 --> 00:01:27.069
Totally different
experience for the person

00:01:27.069 --> 00:01:29.660
who's watching it from outside.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.901
So you're watching this airplane and he's

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:35.231
raging by you, but you
still can't hear a thing.

00:01:35.231 --> 00:01:39.802
And then he'll get four or
five hundred feet past you

00:01:39.802 --> 00:01:43.722
and then suddenly, (jet
engine) this thunder hits you,

00:01:43.722 --> 00:01:46.281
and it just rattles everything.

00:01:46.281 --> 00:01:49.253
And it just compresses your chest.

00:01:49.253 --> 00:01:52.611
It's a little wonky for a half a second.

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:55.321
If you just take this
really quick snapshot,

00:01:55.321 --> 00:01:57.602
“Okay, did I die? I don't think I died.”

00:01:57.602 --> 00:01:58.733
Okay, everything is cool again?”

00:01:58.733 --> 00:02:00.170
“Yeah, everything is cool again.”

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:03.503
And then you continue with your mission.

